<title>FRANCE: Brokerage downgrades Rhone-Poulenc to &quot;neutral&quot;.</title>
<headline>Brokerage downgrades Rhone-Poulenc to &quot;neutral&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. brokerage firm Morgan Stanley said on Friday that it lowered its rating on Rhone-Poulenc shares to &quot;neutral&quot; from &quot;outperform&quot; after the shares reached the firm's benchmark price of 195 francs a share.</p>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc shares were up 1.63 percent to 199.50 francs at 0946 GMT while the CAC-40 was up 0.32 percent.</p>
<p>The share had also rallied on Wednesday after the company stuck to a profit forecast despite a product recall by a subsidiary .</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
